# Mistbreath Elder, ruling 2024-07-26: "If you control creatures other than Mistbreath Elder as its triggered ability resolves, you must
# return one of them to its owner's hand." Nothing is targeted (CR 608.2c). At Bot1's upkeep it controls an Ornithopter and a Memnite
# besides the Elder: it must pick exactly one of them (none, both and the Elder itself are refused, and Bot2's Ornithopter is not a choice);
# Bot1 returns the Memnite, so "if you do" the Elder gets one +1/+1 counter (a 3/3) and the Ornithopter stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mistbreath Elder
Ornithopter
Memnite
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mistbreath Elder.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Choose()
! Bot1.Choose(Memnite; Ornithopter)
! Bot1.Choose(Mistbreath Elder)
! Bot1.Choose(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Mistbreath Elder.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mistbreath Elder.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Mistbreath Elder.Toughness = 3
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
